  - Imaging (x‑ray/MRI) showing advanced osteoarthritis or structural problems likely to benefit from surgery.
  - Recurrent falls or deformity affecting function.
- Items to review with PCP first
  - Current level of pain and function (stairs, walking distance, ADLs).
  - Whether conservative treatments (PT, walking aid, injections, weight loss, meds) have been tried and for how long.
  - Fall risk assessment and review of bone health (consider DEXA for osteoporosis screening).
  - If you’re on or may be started on anticoagulation, mention surgical implications — coordinating timing of procedures and perioperative anticoagulation management is critical.
