A. Questions to ask about atrial fibrillation management
- Do I have AF (or is it suspected)? If yes:
  - What is my current stroke risk score (CHA2DS2-VASc) and what does that mean for anticoagulation? (Note: prior stroke gives 2 points and usually means anticoagulation is recommended unless contraindicated.)
  - Am I currently on anticoagulation? If not, should I start one now? If yes, is it the best choice (warfarin vs DOAC)? Why this one for me?
